<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner wins NOk 350 mln pulp deal.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner wins NOk 350 mln pulp deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Wednesday Kvaerner Pulping Oy in Finland had won an order worth 350 million crowns for a large recovery boiler for PT Indah Kiat Pulp and Paper's Perawang mill in Sumatra, Indonesia.  </p>
<p>Kvaerner said the recovery boiler would be one of the largest in the world with a capacity of 3,300 tonnes of dry solids per day. It wil be delivered at the end of 1998.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
